    "abstract": "In this paper we study a classical Maxwell question on the existence of self-stresses for frameworks, which are called tensegrities. We give a complete answer on geometric conditions of at most $(d+1)$-valent tensegrities in $\\mathbb{R}^d$ both in terms of discrete multiplicative 1-forms and in terms of &#34;meet&#34; and &#34;join&#34; operations in the Grassmann-Cayley algebra.",
    "abstract_method": "arxiv-abs-page",
    "abstract_search_scope": "arxiv",
    "arxiv_title": "Geometric criteria for realizability of tensegrities in higher dimensions",
